experiment:
Positive control (about 10 min). C-free Gray-Scott at Pearson's self-replicating-spot parameters (LITERATURE.md 2.8.1) must give dividing spots.

Main (about 50 min). The three-species system, reconstructed from its reactions (A + 2B -> 3B, B -> P, B + 2C -> 3C, C -> P):
- a_t = DA lap a - a b^2 + r(1-a);
- b_t = DB lap b + a b^2 - k1 b - k2 b c^2;
- c_t = DC lap c + k2 b c^2 - k3 c.
The PDF's equation glyphs did not extract. If spots die, check Virgo 2011, ch. 5.

Setup: Fig. 4 parameters DA = 2e-5, DB = 1e-5, DC = 1e-6, r = 0.0347, k1 = 0.2, k2 = 0.8, k3 = 0.005, on a periodic 2x2 domain at 256^2. Seed spots plus one small C patch; separately, try a noise start.

Measure:
- tailed-spot speed (paper: ~4e-4 per time unit);
- the fraction of duplications in which both daughters keep a tail;
- tailed against tailless share, with and without cataclysms (food zeroed in a random 0.5x0.5 box every 1000 t, in one half only);
- tail acquisitions by contact. Those are contagion under RUBRIC L7, so they count as L5 evidence, not L7.

Run labkit's D and H gates. Record what this pure-Laplacian world scores as the reference arm for Q:owed-laplacian-twins and C:swim-divide-bd.
